<%# locals: (revealed: false) -%>
<%#
  Draft-recovery notice. Render INSIDE a form_with carrying
  data-controller="form-draft" (see the form_draft docs page). Two pieces:

  1. The visible warning chip — navigation-only, hidden until the controller
     reveals it. NOT the announcement path (un-hiding a populated live region
     announces unreliably).
  2. The stable sr-only status region — always present, empty at render; the
     controller writes announcements into it. Announcement strings ride data
     attributes because Stimulus has no I18n.

  `revealed:` exists for previews/render-tests only; production callers use
  the default.

  FORK DIVERGENCE — no `default:` on any t() call. The gem's template ships
  inline defaults, which is right for a gem: a host that has not filed the
  keys still renders text. This app's rule is stricter (ModelRails/NoI18nDefault,
  enforced by erb_lint) because a default silences both i18n gates, so a missing
  key looks healthy forever. Every key here is defined in
  config/locales/en/form_drafts.en.yml. Re-running the add generator restores
  the defaults and fails the push — strip them again.
-%>
<%= tag.div data: { form_draft_target: "notice" },
      hidden: !revealed,
      class: "mb-6 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 rounded-md border border-warning-border bg-warning-surface px-4 py-3" do %>
  <p class="font-medium text-warning">
    <%= t("form_draft.notice") %>
  </p>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
    <button type="button" class="btn-secondary focus-ring"
            data-action="form-draft#recover">
      <%= t("form_draft.recover") %>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="btn-secondary focus-ring"
            data-action="form-draft#discard">
      <%= t("form_draft.discard") %>
    </button>
  </div>
<% end %>
<div data-form-draft-target="status"
     role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" class="sr-only"
     data-found-text="<%= t("form_draft.found") %>"
     data-restored-one-text="<%= t("form_draft.restored_one") %>"
     data-restored-other-text="<%= t("form_draft.restored_other") %>"
     data-restored-partial-text="<%= t("form_draft.restored_partial") %>"
     data-restored-none-text="<%= t("form_draft.restored_none") %>"
     data-discarded-text="<%= t("form_draft.discarded") %>"></div>
